# Per-role override for core canon's record-fields-gate.sh (core issue #66).
# This role's own required-record-fields divergence, preserved explicitly
# now that the local gate copy is deleted (issue-2 action 4). Analogous
# role to RECORD_FIELDS_TERMINAL_STATES in the issue's named example, but
# for required fields rather than terminal states.
#
# ASSUMPTION (flagged in docs/issue-2/reports/implementation/survey.md):
# the exact filename/format core's promoted gate reads per-role config
# from was not verifiable in this tree (core repo not vendored here beyond
# hooks/lib/role-directive.sh and the two gate scripts inspected). This
# file records the value that must survive under whatever mechanism core
# actually reads; rename/reformat to match core's real convention once
# confirmed.
REQUIRED_FIELDS="deal-structure-verdict,term-sheet-outline,partner-id,lifecycle-stage"

# ASSUMPTION (per proposal docs/issue-1/proposals/rulebook-maturation.md,
# item (d)(3)): this sub-section-level requirement is new gate surface,
# not confirmed to be read by core's promoted record-fields-gate.sh. If
# core's gate has no sub-section-level hook, this line documents the
# convention for human PR review to enforce until core ships one (see
# proposal item (d)(5) for the phase-1-side analog of this same gap).
REQUIRED_SUBSECTIONS_term_sheet_outline="purpose,roles-responsibilities,terms,governance,kpis,dispute-resolution,exit-termination"
